-- title:
--   Integrality of the H₁-moduli ring over A[j₀]
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes with $\ell \ge 5$, let $M' \ne 0$ be a natural number, and assume that the images of $\ell$ and of $M'$ in $A$ are units. Three equivariance hypotheses are imposed, for all $A$-algebras $T$: `hℓ` says that the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point condition `IsGamma1Point` (a point $(x_P,y_P)$ on the affine Weierstrass equation with $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell)(x_P)=0$ and second coordinate pair equal to the first) is preserved by the variable-change action on `LevelPData`; `hM` says that `IsGamma0PowAt` (the two-torsion kernel condition when $p^k=2$, otherwise the monic degree-$\varphi(p^k)/2$ cyclic-kernel-generator condition) is preserved under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; and `hL` says that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` is preserved likewise. Further data: a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on the Proj models of projective Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant, assumed chord–tangent (its points functor matches the affine point group over fields) and origin-normalised; a transport $\mathcal T$ of raw Drinfeld pairs along $A$-algebra maps and variable changes, compatible with $q$-level Drinfeld bases, satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; and the pins `hVC`, `hCO` providing graded variable-change and coefficient homomorphisms of the Proj model rings dominating the irrelevant ideal. Finally let $P_0$ be any abstract package representing the moduli datum `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓ M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`, that is a commutative $A$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point that represents the functor of $\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma_1(\ell)$-plus-Drinfeld-$q$-level structures with the $\Gamma_1$-link divisibility, taken modulo variable change, with $B_0$ of finite type over $A$. Then $B_0$ is integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by the single element `P₀.j₀`, the $j$-invariant of the universal point.
--
--   This is the properness-type finiteness statement for the moduli problem of level $\Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell)$ together with a Drinfeld $q$-basis: the coarse coordinate $j_0$ already controls the whole coordinate ring integrally, with no assumption that $2$ or $3$ be invertible in $A$. It is used downstream in the analysis of the minimal primes of $B_0$ and of the fibres of the $j$-line map for this level structure.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_isIntegral_adjoin_j0_levelModuliPackageAbs_rigidDataH1Pow.lean

